: true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-cap30-19-off/omp-19/cells/with/trig-omp-multistep/22/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/a95d432f7bc115e3b642c41ee48344d81c6221c7/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` truncates a float (`19.99 * 100 == 1998.9999999999998` \u2192 `1998`). Fix by converting via the decimal string representation and rounding half-up.\npytest isn't installed, so run the test functions directly (both test files).\nFixed. The bug was in `ledger/currency.py`, in `to_cents`. It computed `int(amount * 100)`, and float math is slightly off for some prices: `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999999999998`, which `int()` cuts down to `1998`. The same thing turned `0.29` into 28 cents and `4.35` into 434, which broke all four tests.\n\n`to_cents` now converts the amount through `Decimal(str(amount))` and rounds to the nearest cent, with exact halves going up. So float error can no longer drop a cent. The other modules already did everything in whole cents, so nothing else needed to change.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here, so I imported both test files with `python3` and ran every `test_*` function directly. All 4 tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and the one in `tests/test_report.py` passed. They haven't been run through pytest itself.\n\n**One behaviour change:** an amount with more tha